---
title: "07f  States of one cash advance, from grant to liquidation"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: a cash advance leaves the Treasury before any delivery is accepted. How does the government ensure that the money is later accounted for?
  %% IDEA: a cash advance is money given to a named officer, who is personally accountable for it until he or she presents proof of how it was spent (liquidation) and returns the rest.
  %% SOURCES: accountable officers must be bonded, and BTr administers the bonding [EO449]. Weakness reported: a part of the advances, in particular advances to government corporations, was not liquidated at the end of 2023 (indicator 27.3, score C) [PEFA2025].
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: all states and time limits in this diagram follow my recollection of COA Circular No. 97-002 (rules on cash advances). I did not open that circular. Check it before relying on a time limit.

  state "Requested (voucher for a specific purpose)" as REQ
  state "Granted to a bonded accountable officer" as GR
  state "In use (officer pays and collects receipts)" as USE
  state "Liquidation report submitted with receipts" as LIQ
  state "Liquidated (accounting verifies, journal entry, expense recorded)" as DONE
  state "Unspent cash returned (official receipt)" as RET
  state "Overdue (not liquidated within the time limit)" as OVD
  state "Demand letter, then salary withheld" as DEM
  state "Disallowed, or charged to the officer" as DIS

  [*] --> REQ: head of unit
  REQ --> GR: approved voucher, no earlier advance remains unliquidated
  GR --> USE: only for the stated purpose
  USE --> LIQ: officer, within the time limit for the kind of advance
  USE --> RET: purpose fulfilled, cash remains
  RET --> LIQ
  LIQ --> DONE: accountant and auditor find the documents complete and proper
  LIQ --> DIS: documents missing or expense not allowed
  USE --> OVD: time limit passes
  OVD --> DEM: accountant, auditor
  DEM --> LIQ: officer complies
  DEM --> DIS: officer does not comply
  DONE --> [*]
  DIS --> [*]: recovery from the officer (chapter 09)
